#: inc/glossary.php:211
msgid "A taxi built or converted to carry a passenger seated in their wheelchair, with a ramp or hoist, wheelchair restraints and a seatbelt for the passenger."
msgstr ""

#: inc/glossary.php:212
msgid "A larger taxi that seats up to 11 passengers. Many maxi taxis are also wheelchair accessible, but not all — ask for a wheelchair accessible vehicle when you book."
msgstr ""

#: inc/glossary.php:213
msgid "A Victorian Government program that pays part of the taxi fare for eligible people with a severe and permanent disability. Members show their MPTP card to the driver and pay the rest of the fare."
msgstr ""

#: inc/glossary.php:214
msgid "A payment the Victorian Government makes to drivers of wheelchair accessible taxis for each trip with a passenger who travels in their wheelchair. It is not charged to the passenger."
msgstr ""

#: inc/glossary.php:215
msgid "Money in an NDIS plan that helps a participant travel to work, study, therapy and community activities when they cannot use public transport without substantial difficulty. It can usually pay for taxi trips."
msgstr ""

#: inc/glossary.php:215
msgid "[CONFIRM against current NDIS guidelines.]"
msgstr ""

#: inc/glossary.php:216
